    "point": "§FS-declarations.checks.declaration-near-miss.1",
    "authoredFrom": "Read from the case's input bytes: grund.toml (version 1 and nothing else, so the default kinds, scan and `[id] format = \"{kind}-{number}-{slug}\"`, §FS-config.3.4.4, §FS-config.3.5, §FS-config.3.2). The default scan reads docs and src with the hs, lisp and lua extensions. FS-001-alpha is a lone heading line, its body and lead empty (§FS-list.3.4.1), listed by the FS index with its anchor. Each source file opens a comment block on a line-comment prefix form, `-- |` in A.hs line 3, `;;` in a.lisp line 1 and `---` in a.lua line 1 (§FS-languages.prefixes.forms), in declaration position (§FS-declarations.line), with an FS-kind token, the declaration colon and a title, whose ID lacks the `-NNN-` the effective format requires: each is a near miss (§FS-declarations.checks.declaration-near-miss.1, .2) and one error at its heading line, naming the token as written and the default template (§FS-declarations.checks.declaration-near-miss.4, .5). Each still declares (§FS-config.3.2.5): kind FS, title `per §FS-001-alpha`, a body that is empty because the block ends at its heading line and the code below is no part of it (§FS-show.2.3.1), and a null anchor (§FS-show.3.1.3.1). The marked FS-001-alpha on each near-miss heading is a citation from that declaration, at the heading's line, owned by that declaration under no section (§FS-citations.recognized.title-lines, §FS-cover.6.2), so with the index entry FS-001-alpha has four sites and is used (§FS-check.4.1); nothing cites the three near misses, so each is unused at its heading (§FS-check.4.1). Source declarations owe no index entry (§FS-check.3.18). The report is ordered by path, line and message, the site-less version caution first (§FS-errors.4.1, §FS-check.2.1.1). Fmt rewrites no source file and never a declaration heading line (§FS-fmt.6.1, §FS-fmt.2.3), and the index entry already links where the cross-reference writer would (§FS-fmt.6.3), so it changes nothing. The golden pins check: exit 1, the six located findings on stdout and the version caution on stderr. FS-404 is the absent control.",
